figdown 0.1 block
# `OPTION-POSITION-PARSING`: an option may appear ANYWHERE on a directive line —
# `splitOpts` extracts `key=` tokens by shape and the positional arguments
# close up behind them. Two directives contradicted that: `bundle` and
# `threshold` (spelled `guide` until this release) tested quotedness on the RAW
# token stream while reading the value from the option-stripped one, so an
# option BEFORE the label shifted the indices apart and rejected a legal line
# ("bad member ..." / "threshold needs a quoted label"). `band` joined the
# label-bearing set (`BAND-LABEL-STATUS`) and obeys the same rule.
# Quotedness is now carried `pos`-aligned, so the two behave like everyone
# else. This case pins option-before-label on all six label-bearing directives
# it applies to; its subject is the generic option/positional rule, not the
# demoted constructs it uses to prove it (STATUS.txt criterion).
class fill=#e0f2fe c1 "Fabric"
plane z-index=2 L1 "Overlay"
node fill=#fef9c3 a "A"
node b "B"
group fill=#f1f5f9 g "Pod"
external plane=L1 e "Uplink"
edge a -- b
bundle stroke=#0ea5e9 t1 "LAG" a--b
threshold in=g "Threshold" offset=50%
band in=g "Shared" fill=#dcfce7 15..35%
